From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenSec <contactus@opensec.in>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:25:56 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Pi-Bolt: JavaScriptCore's ahead-of-time compiler

JavaScriptCore's changes for Pi-Bolt's executables, on Linux x86-64 and macOS ARM64:

- An x86-64 back end for ahead-of-time code, and the runtime work it needs.
- Optimizations: inlining of helpers held in module constants and of methods by name, variables
  narrowed in loops, stores cached by computed key, integral doubles boxed as int32, integer
  remainders; a size limit for what is compiled.
- Correctness: a write barrier after every Structure transition; frames of ahead-of-time code make no
  CodeBlock during a collection; string type checks; endsWith() of long strings; closure environments
  that stay when a name is only found as the code runs; image builds that are the same every time and
  free of a race between their threads; a build that stops, and says why, when a function is declined.
- ARM64 and Darwin: 64-bit constants told apart from addresses, callee numbers loaded with movz and
  movk, unicode regular expressions in image code, a map of the image's functions, stubs and regular
  expressions.
- Intl on Darwin: the plain language tags of ICU's lists of locales made without ICU.
